      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-159834",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose $X_{1}, X_{2}, \u2026, X_{8}$ is an I.I.D random sample with $X_{i}\u223cExp(\u03b8)$ and unknown rate parameter $\u03b8$. For a particular sample $x_{1}, x_{2}, \u2026, x_{8}$, you're given that\n$\u2211_(i = 1)^(8)x_{i} = 28.4$.\nGiven that the log-likelihood function of the sample is\n$l(\u03b8) = a\\ln \u03b8 + b\u03b8$,\nwhat is the value of $a + b$?\n\n*Hint: The probability density function for an exponential random variable is given by*\n$f(x) = \u03b8e^{- \u03b8x}, x \\ge 0$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
