      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-159835",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose $X_{1}, X_{2}, X_{3}$ is an I.I.D random sample with $X_{i}\u223cExp(\u03b8)$ and unknown rate parameter $\u03b8$. The log-likelihood function of the sample $5.1, 4.2, 6.3$ is\n$l(\u03b8) = a\\ln \u03b8 + b\u03b8$.\nWhat is the value of $a + b$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
